Manual review findings:
  - No raw stack traces printed to stdout/stderr in production source.
  - No System.exit calls in webhook/converter code.
  - No hardcoded passwords, tokens, or private key literals.
  - ReloadableSslContext uses an empty char[] for the in-memory KeyStore password,
    which is acceptable because the keystore is generated in memory and never persisted.
  - AdmissionHandler and ConversionHandler catch RuntimeException and return a
    failed admission/conversion response; this is fail-closed behavior, not an anti-pattern.
  - EchoMutatingWebhook builds JSON Patch via string concatenation; while brittle,
    it does not match the listed anti-patterns and the constant value is safe.

